# RR13 bounded regular snapshot admission

SnapshotStore now requires an absolute root without parent components, rejects symlink roots and ancestors, and pins an open directory descriptor to retain root inode identity. Linux x86_64 uses checked NONBLOCK/NOFOLLOW flags and rejects final symlinks, directories and special files. Opened and post-read regular-file identities, lengths and modification/change timestamps must match; reads reserve the admitted size and refuse before extending past it. Root identity is checked across operations. Other platforms explicitly refuse. Parents must remain stable; these checks are not descriptor-relative openat protection, a hostile-writer snapshot, arbitrary device-substitution safety or a regular-disk deadline.

The effective snapshot read/output cap is 4 MiB, matching the inherited RR04 model admission ceiling. The old 16 MiB outer read guard could not make >4 MiB models admissible on this snapshot; refusal now happens earlier. Save uses RR04 bounded output before SnapshotIo staging while preserving one write/sync/publish/directory-sync/remove sequence and hard-link no-replace behavior. Directory sync also uses the nonblocking directory opener, covering a root-to-FIFO swap after publication. Trusted injected I/O can still perform a side effect before returning an error; such failures may have published data. No cleanup, retry, physical power-loss or durability guarantee is invented.

The immutable prerequisite FIFO test blocks and is killed and waited after three seconds; original source and failure remain retained. Final qualification includes real owned FIFO and replacement-race children, explicit root/ancestor/final-file policies, exact/over-limit bytes, normal save/reopen and controlled write/publication/directory-sync failures. All 26 cases pass: three new race unit, eight new integration, two inherited connected and thirteen inherited fault cases. Exact commands are in the captures and plan ledger. Existing fault semantics and retained staged artifacts remain visible. Scoped formatting, all-target Clippy and independent source review pass on exact committed bytes. No factory feature, native PostgreSQL, browser or full application acceptance is claimed.

Implementation commit: `1e09637714b78e23297e93b43084027491429ac0`. [Executed and committed inputs](executed-source-binding.json), [independent review](independent-review.json), [captures](captures/). Status: **LOCALLY_VERIFIED_BOUNDED / NOT_ACCEPTED**. Land prerequisites, retarget and requalify; never merge into feature or temporary snapshot bases. All prior holds remain held.
